    {
      "id": "p0264-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "As we've seen, Underta/e's Japanese localization has impressed Japanese players, game developers, and critics alike. The localization's success has even inspired others to follow Toby's path of turning a simple hobby into a full fledged career, much as EarthBound's Japanese-to-English localization did for Toby nearly thirty years ago. Games are usually localized to make money, but now we're seeing how localization can start a cycle of inspiration that crosses the language barrier.",
        "raw": "As we've seen, Underta/e's Japanese localization has impressed Japanese\nplayers, game developers, and critics alike. The localization's success has even\ninspired others to follow Toby's path of turning a simple hobby into a full\nfledged career, much as EarthBound's Japanese-to-English localization did for\nToby nearly thirty years ago. Games are usually localized to make money, but\nnow we're seeing how localization can start a cycle of inspiration that crosses\nthe language barrier.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.28888384,
          0.09447143,
          0.88742365,
          0.215
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.2868563,
          0.09375714,
          0.89985247,
          0.21607143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5,
          6,
          7,
          8
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "我们已经看到，《Undertale》的日文本地化赢得了日本玩家、开发者与评论者的赞赏。它的成功甚至鼓舞了其他人，让他们沿着 Toby 的道路，把普通爱好变成正式事业——正如近三十年前，《EarthBound》的日译英曾启发 Toby 一样。游戏本地化通常为了赚钱，但现在我们也看到了，它如何开启跨越语言障碍、不断传递灵感的循环。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 17,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          },
          {
            "start": 93,
