    {
      "id": "p0264-b007",
      "kind": "caption",
      "source": {
        "text": "Lancer has a unique \"ho ho ho\" laugh in both the English and Japanese scripts. In English, \"ho ho ho\" is closely associated with Santa Claus' laugh, but in Japanese, \"ho ho ho\" is more closely associated with the laughter of snooty rich ladies. As such, Lancer is compared to Santa Claus in the English script and a snooty old hag in the Japanese script",
        "raw": "Lancer has a unique \"ho ho ho\" laugh in both the English and Japanese scripts. In English, \"ho\nho ho\" is closely associated with Santa Claus' laugh, but in Japanese, \"ho ho ho\" is more closely\nassociated with the laughter of snooty rich ladies. As such, Lancer is compared to Santa Claus in\nthe English script and a snooty old hag in the Japanese script",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29261451,
          0.83638571,
          0.88930926,
          0.89337143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
